  "sourceUrl": "https://techspecs.ui.com/unifi/switching/usw-pro-48",
  "notes": "PoE, read 2026-11-28. `https://dl.ui.com/ds/usw-pro-48_ds.pdf` (HTTP 200, `application/pdf`, 447,392 B, text layer) prints **Networking interface = (48) GbE RJ45 ports / (4) 1/10G SFP+ ports**, **Power method = Universal input, 100-240V AC, 50/60 Hz; USP RPS DC input, 11.5V DC, 5.22A**, **Power supply = AC/DC, internal, 60W** and **Max. power consumption = 60W**. There is no PoE line, no PoE budget and no class anywhere on the sheet: this is the non-PoE Switch Pro 48, powered from the mains and optionally from the USP RPS DC bus. The 48 copper ports therefore carry `poeIn: false`. Without it `isPoePd()` in `engine/media.js` matched `unifi` in the label (\\\"UniFi Pro 48\\\") and inferred a 12.95 W 802.3af draw on every socket - **621.6 W** asked of whatever PSE the lab cabled it to, on a switch whose own supply is 60 W. Same correction as `uxg-pro.json` and `udm-pro-max.json` (PR #2111). The `techspecs.ui.com` page named in `sourceUrl` is a client-rendered shell here (HTTP 200, 0 bytes over the wire), so the PDF is the figure of record."
}
